## Fonts - SIL Open Font License 1.1

Both families are bundled in `src/renderer/src/fonts/` as WOFF2 variable fonts.
The files are byte-for-byte as distributed by Google Fonts (the standard `latin`
and `latin-ext` subsets); they have not been modified or re-subset here, so the
"Quicksand" Reserved Font Name is not implicated.

  - Baloo 2 - Copyright 2019 The Baloo 2 Project Authors
    https://github.com/EkType/Baloo2
    Full license: src/renderer/src/fonts/OFL-Baloo2.txt

  - Quicksand - Copyright 2011 The Quicksand Project Authors,
    with Reserved Font Name "Quicksand".
    https://github.com/andrew-paglinawan/QuicksandFamily
    Full license: src/renderer/src/fonts/OFL-Quicksand.txt

The SIL OFL permits bundling and redistribution inside an application, including
commercially, provided the license text accompanies the fonts - which is why the
two OFL files above ship in the repository and inside the packaged app.

## Bundled software dependencies

Bileog ships only four npm packages at runtime; everything else in the
dependency tree is either compiled into the renderer bundle by Vite or is
build-time tooling that is excluded from the packaged app.

  - better-sqlite3   - MIT - Copyright (c) 2017 Joshua Wise
  - bindings         - MIT
  - file-uri-to-path - MIT
  - nanoid           - MIT

  SQLite itself is compiled into the better-sqlite3 native addon and is in the
  public domain (the SQLite authors disclaim copyright).

  Electron - MIT - bundles Chromium and Node.js. Chromium is BSD-3-Clause and
  its own dependencies carry a range of permissive licenses; the complete set is
  reproduced verbatim in the packaged app at:

      Contents/Resources/licenses/LICENSES.chromium.html
      Contents/Resources/licenses/LICENSE.electron

A full audit of the dependency tree (440 packages, production and development)
found no copyleft or reciprocal licenses - no GPL, LGPL, AGPL, MPL, EPL or
SSPL - and no package lacking a declared license. All are MIT, ISC, BSD, Apache
2.0 or equivalently permissive, and all are compatible with distributing this
project under the MIT license.

